; A constructor pattern must belong to the type the match is over,
; and a match over a placeholder-typed value is still exhaustiveness
; checked.
;
; Nothing compared the two until 2026-08-21. `checkCtorPattern`
; resolved the constructor, checked its arity, bound its fields, and
; never looked at the scrutinee's type, so a `Color` constructor
; matched an `Int`, a `Shape`, or a signature's rigid `a` - and with
; the scrutinee never a data type, exhaustiveness never ran either.
; The QA sweep's `g` below checked OK and answered 0 for both
; `(g 42)` and `(g "hello")` through the result cell's zeroed
; contents, MM-VAL-9b's shape one type variable further out.
;
;   line 33: `(Red)` against a rigid `a`          AX3004, expected Color
;   line 36: `(Red)` against an `Int`             AX3004
;   line 39: `(Red)` against a `Shape`            AX3004
;   line 42: a string literal against an `Int`    AX3004, expected String
;   line 46: a lambda parameter - a minted `_tN` - matched against
;            `Red` and `Green` with `Blue` missing   AX3005
;   line 53: a string literal NESTED in `Some` over `(Option Int)`
;            AX3004, expected String - the constructor's `a` is
;            instantiated at the scrutinee's `Int` (`ctorPatEnv`),
;            not minted fresh; with a fresh placeholder this passed
;            `check` and the content comparison dereferenced 5
;
; `ok` emits nothing: `(Option a)` fits `Some`/`None`, because only the
; HEAD names are compared (`ctorPatFits`) and the arguments are what
; `bindPatternArgs` instantiates.
(data Color
  (Red)
  (Green)
  (Blue))

(data Shape
  (Circle Int)
  (Square Int))

(:: g (-> a Int))

(fn (g v)
  (match v
    ((Red) 1)
    (_ 0)
  )
)

(:: h (-> Int Int))

(fn (h n)
  (match n
    ((Red) 1)
    (_ 0)
  )
)

(:: k (-> Shape Int))

(fn (k s)
  (match s
    ((Red) 1)
    ((Circle r) r)
    (_ 0)
  )
)

(:: lit (-> Int Int))

(fn (lit n)
  (match n
    ("hello" 1)
    (_ 0)
  )
)

(:: ph Int)

(fn (ph)
  (let ((f 
    (lambda (x)
      (match x
        ((Red) 1)
        ((Green) 2)
      )
    )
  ))
    (f Blue)
  )
)

(:: ok (-> (Option a) Int))

(fn (ok o)
  (match o
    ((Some x) 1)
    ((None) 0)
  )
)

(:: nested (-> (Option Int) Int))

(fn (nested o)
  (match o
    ((Some "x") 1)
    (_ 0)
  )
)

(:: main Int)

(fn (main) 0)
